use std
use ffi
use amni-drive
into drive_abi.amni
lang amni
C-ABI shared library exports for Amni-Drive's Helium + Gold native core (`libamni_drive_he.so` on Android NDK). Imports `look`, `layout`, `aap`, `gate`, `scrub`, `drum3d`, and `cockpit_render`.
Exported function `he_drive_gate` takes `drive_state`, `gate_on`, `passenger`, and `category` as 32-bit integers and returns `gate::resolve_gate` with `gate_on` nonzero and `passenger` nonzero as a 32-bit integer.
Exported function `he_drive_haversine` takes `lat1`, `lon1`, `lat2`, and `lon2` as 64-bit floats and returns `gate::haversine_meters(lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2)` as a 64-bit float.
Exported function `he_drive_bearing` takes `lat1`, `lon1`, `lat2`, and `lon2` as 64-bit floats and returns `gate::bearing_deg(lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2)` as a 32-bit float.
Exported function `he_drive_palette_color` takes `preset_idx` and `slot` as 32-bit integers, `custom_acc` as an unsigned 32-bit integer, and `high_contrast` as a 32-bit integer, returning an unsigned 32-bit ARGB color from `look::build_palette` at clamped `preset_idx`.
Exported function `he_drive_type_metric` takes `screen_w`, `screen_h`, and `user_scale` as 32-bit floats and `slot` as a 32-bit integer, returning the matching field of `look::car_type_scale(screen_w, screen_h, user_scale)`.
Exported function `he_drive_cockpit_valid` takes `screen_w`, `screen_h`, and `user_scale` as 32-bit floats and `layout_id`, `dock_mode`, and `swap` as 32-bit integers, returning `layout::validate_cockpit` of `layout::compute_cockpit` as a 32-bit integer.
Exported function `he_drive_scrub_buf` takes `in_ptr` as an unsigned integer address, `in_len` as a 32-bit integer, `out_ptr` as an unsigned integer address, and `out_cap` as a 32-bit integer, returning written byte count as a 32-bit integer using `ffi::bytes`, `scrub::scrub_text`, and `ffi::write`.
Exported function `he_drive_load_font` takes `font_ptr` as an unsigned integer address and `font_len` as a 32-bit integer, returning 1 if `cockpit_render::load_font_bytes(ffi::bytes(font_ptr, font_len))` succeeds else 0.
Exported function `he_drive_render_rgba` takes `out_ptr` as an unsigned integer address and `w`, `h`, `preset_idx`, `layout_id`, `dock_mode`, `speed_mph`, `temp_f`, and `active_btn` as 32-bit integers, plus `roll_deg` as a 32-bit float, returning the byte count written as a 32-bit integer by calling `cockpit_render::draw_cockpit_at` at clamped `preset_idx` and writing `canvas.px` via `ffi::write`.
Exported function `he_drive_drum_step` takes `angle_deg`, `vel_deg`, and `dt` as 32-bit floats, `dragging` as a 32-bit integer, and `out_ptr` as an unsigned integer address pointing to 12 bytes (three little-endian 32-bit floats/ints). Build a `drum3d::DrumState` with `angle_deg`, `vel_deg`, `active_idx = 0`, and `dragging` nonzero; call `drum3d::drum_step(st, dt)`; pack `st.angle_deg` (32-bit IEEE float bits), `st.vel_deg` (32-bit IEEE float bits), and `st.active_idx` (32-bit int) into 12 little-endian bytes and write them to `out_ptr` via `ffi::write`. Return `st.active_idx`.
Function `main` does nothing.
